Remove obsolete bulk transfers for migrated ordinary backend facts. Delete ordinary-state TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot machinery, TuiSubmitResult::state_snapshot payloads, snapshot-bearing keybinding/reload results, app builders and apply helpers when their migrated responsibilities have replacements. Preserve both deferred history/streaming and deferred interactive exchanges (permission/question, plugin, subagent/control/inspector, branch-confirmation and related request/completion), including necessary existing protocol state and dependencies. Shared plumbing may require minimal compatibility adjustments, not protocol replacement. Do not remove behavior to satisfy a type-name criterion or introduce a journal, history-access or popup API before the user's separate design.

Reduce runtime options to frontend initialization dependencies, local UI configuration and required action endpoints, plus precisely documented existing history and interactive-exchange interfaces. No duplicate initial or callback-delivered display copy of migrated ordinary backend facts may remain. Audit TUI includes/signatures and isolate migrated backend bindings behind src/ava/frontend or app/tui without cycles; infrastructure is ava::frontend, not app::frontend or core. Retain narrow committed-identity control reads at serialized transition boundaries, independently of consumed display flags. Record pre-existing dependencies needed by deferred paths instead of rewriting those APIs to satisfy a blanket decoupling rule; these exceptions do not authorize new unrelated backend access.

All in-scope ordinary backend facts use UnlockedData notifications and projection refreshes; their action results carry errors/control rather than replacement state. Pure appearance/interaction, themes/keybindings/preview, selector controls and drafts remain tui-thread-local without locks/UnlockedData; draft crosses only as a submitted string. Audit every producer/consumer: no Snapshot or renamed bypass for migrated active-agent/directory/model/provider/variant/token facts. Verify exact preserved history and interactive paths and their authority/order tests. Do not move pending prompts or protocol-specific state into UnlockedData, and do not create stubs without explicit agreement.

Deletion must respect explicit exclusions, not just history: TrustState and its existing on-demand /settings Workspace/ProjectTrustSnapshot delivery remain unwrapped; /models and /scoped-models retain their popup list/result contracts and unchanged optional scope semantics. Preserve image/editor/Mermaid APIs and protocol synchronization. Catalog/resource/todo records require the individual approvals in /04 and /05 before their replacement transports can be removed; do not invent missing canonical types to satisfy cleanup.

Keep current FrontEnd::register_frontend_data and typed initialize_frontend_state, including its Session read access. Do not implement the deferred FrontendDataIndices/SessionFrontendBinding alternative to eliminate headers. Preserve stable nested SessionStoreOptions registration, no duplicate backend SessionIdentity, nested prompt mode/vector ownership, whole Directories/Stats snapshots and metadata-only agent projection. No speculative typed identity/path/mode/count/scope getters or additional canonical copies. Source comments must distinguish exact snapshots from derived caches, and canonical names/refresh methods follow current user-edited code rather than historical proposal spellings.
